  "articleBody": "Discovering a leak from your brand-new kitchen faucet can be really frustrating, but don't panic! The first thing to do is quickly turn off the water supply to the sink. There should be shut-off valves typically located underneath the sink in the cabinet. Once the water is off, you can start to investigate. Often, a leak can be due to a loose connection at the supply lines or the drain assembly. Carefully check all the nuts and fittings to see if any need a gentle tightening. Avoid overtightening, as this can damage components. Another common culprit is improper sealing around the base of the faucet where it meets the countertop. If the sealant isn't applied correctly or if there's a gap, water can seep through. If the leak persists after checking these basic points, or if you're uncomfortable troubleshooting plumbing connections, it's definitely time to call in a professional. Issues with old or nonstandard plumbing, or when the leak's source isn't obvious, really benefit from expert attention. HH Remodeling LLC can diagnose and fix these problems efficiently, ensuring your installation is watertight.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
